## Markup Reference

Processed client-side by `processStudyMarkup()` in `views/reader-view.js`:

| Syntax | Purpose | Renders as |
|--------|---------|------------|
| `$wings` | Symbol ref | Link showing "WINGS" (from SYMBOL_DICTIONARY) or capitalized key |
| `$[name]` | Symbol ref preserving display text | Link showing "name" (original case) — for Scripture quotes |
| `H6738` | Strong's Hebrew number | Button linking to Strong's panel |
| `G4639` | Strong's Greek number | Button linking to Strong's panel |
| `Ps 91:1` | Verse ref (abbreviated book) | Clickable link to Bible reader |
| `[seven](/reader/numbers/7)` | Number study link | Markdown link to number study |

**Inside Scripture quotes:** Use `$[key]` to link a word without changing the display text. KJV text stays faithful.

**Strong's in prose:** Write `H6738 *tsel*` — number auto-links, transliteration is regular markdown.

**Verse abbreviations:** Use any abbreviation from `bible.js` BOOK_NAME_MAP. Must include chapter:verse with colon.

**Name substitution:** "the LORD" automatically becomes user's preferred name — no special markup needed.

